>>Luck is a number, from -10 to +10, let's say, with negative being 'bad'
>>and positive being 'good.'  Every hundred turns or so, luck moves one
>>step towards zero...  Having a luckstone just affects how your luck times
>>out.  A cursed stone lets good luck time out, but not bad luck.  An
>>uncursed stone freezes your luck, wherever it may be.
>
>Another luck-related question.  In the discussion on cockatrice stoning
>probabilities, a few times the provision was made "unless it's new moon".
>I was under the impression that new moon just meant an initially negative
>luck stat.  Is it actually something that influences the whole game?
If it's new moon / full moon, the 'zero' mentioned above is increased/decreased
by one, so if it's new moon, your luck will move towards -1 instead of 0.
If it's full moon, and you're having a uncursed/blessed luckstone, your luck
will move towards +4 instead.

>Is new
>moon/full moon calculated from my computer's date?  I always seem to get new/
>full moons in long streaks.  And I must say, I seemed to be extremely unlucky
>a few weeks ago, with lotsa new moons =)
>Rob
Yep, it's calculated from your computers date. That means, that if you're on a
single-user system, you could change the time to simulate full moon... (Of
course it is possible on multi-user system too if you have permissions, but it
is not recommended!)

